.TH WAVE-UPGRADE 1 "" "MacWave" "MacWave Manual"

.SH NAME
wave-upgrade \- Install the latest version of a package, or of every installed package with --all. Versions coexist, so the old ones stay until -X removes them.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wave upgrade <package> | wave upgrade \-\-all
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install the latest version of a package, or of every installed package
with --all. Versions coexist, so the old ones stay until -X removes
them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Upgrade every installed package that has a newer version
.TP
.B \-X, \-\-remove\-old\-versions
Also remove the versions older than the one just installed
.TP
.B \-C, \-\-continue
Resume an interrupted download (like curl -C -)
.TP
.B \-\-proxy <string>
HTTP/HTTPS proxy (e.g. http://127.0.0.1:8080)
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-ssl
Skip SSL certificate verification (insecure)
.TP
.B \-\-limit\-rate <string>
Limit download speed (e.g. 200K, 1M, 5M)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-time <string>
Total time limit for the request (40s, 1min, 1min20s, 2h; bare numbers
are seconds)
.TP
.B \-\-connect\-timeout <string>
Give up if the handshake takes longer (like curl)
.TP
.B \-\-content\-time <string>
Give up if no data arrives for this long
.TP
.B \-F, \-\-force
Upgrade anyway when the package declares a newer macOS than this machine
runs
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wave upgrade jq
wave upgrade jq -X
wave upgrade --all
wave upgrade jq --remove-old-versions --max-time=2min
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
wave(1)
